    "reasoning_content": "I now have a lot of information. Let me note key facts:\n\n**GISMo / facebookresearch/gismo (Meta AI):**\n- Authors: Bahare Fatemi (Google Research), Quentin Duval, Rohit Girdhar, Michal Drozdzal, Adriana Romero-Soriano (Meta AI).\n- Code at github.com/facebookresearch/gismo, archived Nov 1, 2024 (read-only).\n- GISMo has three components: ingredient encoder (IE, GIN layers), context encoder (CE), ingredient substitution decoder (ISD).\n- The ingredient encoder uses GIN layers with an optional embedding layer (for one-hot ingredient features).\n- Embedding dimension: need to check the config. The paper's supplementary material has details. Rita reimplemented with 300 dim. Let me check the gismo config to find the embedding dimension.\n- Recipe1MSubs: 49,044 train, 10,729 val, 10,747 test.\n- GISMo results: MRR 31.51, Hit@1 20.56 (test).\n- FlavorGraph: 6,653 food ingredient nodes, 1,645 flavor molecule nodes. Ingredient vocabulary 6,653.\n\nThe card targets the \"ingredient-encoder embedding width\" axis (64-512 dimension). This maps directly to the GISMo ingredient encoder (IE) GIN layer hidden dimension / embedding width.\n\nI should check the gismo config to see the embedding dimension used. Let me look at the conf directory.\n\n**Rita 2024 / Imperial College / iAnalytica:**\n- Authors: Luís Rita, Joshua Southern, Ivan Laponogov, Kyle Higgins, Kirill Veselkov (Imperial College London).\n- Fine-tuned GPT-3.5-Turbo, DaVinci-002, TinyLlama-1.1B on Recipe1MSubs.\n- Hit@1: baseline 34.53 (their GISMo reimplementation on original dataset), improved to 38.03 with GPT-3.5.\n- Repo: https://bitbucket.org/iAnalytica/ingredient-substitution\n- They re-ran GISMo with embedding dimension 300, two GCN layers with 300 hidden units.\n- Funding: ERC Hyperfoods, ERC LEMAN, UKRI, etc. (Veselkov's Hyperfoods project is about phytochemically enriched food - relevant to sustainability/health).\n\nThe card's research question is specifically about whether increasing capacity (embedding width) of the GISMo-style ranker improves Hit@1. This is directly relevant to:\n1. The GISMo project (Meta) - they set the embedding dimension and never swept width.\n2. The Veselkov lab / iAnalytica (Rita et al.) - they reimplemented GISMo at 300 dim and compared to LLMs; a width sweep would tell them whether their GISMo baseline was under-parameterized (i.e., whether the LLM advantage is really \"LLM magic\" vs. capacity).\n\nBoth are good candidates. Let me verify the embedding dimension in the gismo code, and check the supplementary material.\n\nLet me also check the third candidate: a company or consortium for industrial ingredient replacement for sustainability. The card is explicitly framed around \"industrial food ingredient replacement for sustainability.\" Let me think about whether there's a relevant industrial programme.\n\nCandidates:\n- **NotCo** (Chile/US) - uses \"Giuseppe\" AI for plant-based ingredient substitution. But they do plant-based food formulation, not recipe substitution ranking on Recipe1MSubs.\n- **Climax Foods** - AI for plant-based ingredient discovery.\n- **Plant Jammer** - uses AI/LLMs for recipe ingredient substitution (Danish). They actually do ingredient substitution in recipes at scale.\n\nBut the card's result is specifically about the GISMo/Recipe1MSubs benchmark. The most direct \"programmes doing this work now\" are:\n1. Meta AI's GISMo (facebookresearch/gismo) - open-source project.\n2. Imperial College Veselkov lab / iAnalytica (Rita et al. 2024) - the Hyperfoods programme (phytochemical enrichment), which uses ingredient substitution.\n\nActually, the \"Hyperfoods\" ERC project is quite relevant to \"food ingredient replacement for sustainability/health.\" Let me check Hyperfoods.\n\nAlso the card mentions \"src_gismo_sizes\" and \"src_gismo_gismo\" and \"src_llm\" as sources. These correspond to:\n- src_gismo_sizes: GISMo paper sizes (embedding dims? FlavorGraph nodes)\n- src_gismo_gismo: GISMo official code\n- src_llm: Rita 2024 paper\n\nLet me check the Hyperfoods project and iAnalytica to understand the \"industrial programme\" angle. Also, is there a consortium? The Veselkov lab has DreamLab/Vodafone Foundation citizen science.\n\nLet me do a couple more searches/fetches to:\n1. Find the gismo embedding dimension in the code/config (to describe the step precisely).\n2. Check the iAnalytica bitbucket repo for whether a width sweep was done.\n3. Check the Hyperfoods project page.\n\nLet me fetch the gismo conf directory and the Bitbucket repo.\n\nActually, the Bitbucket repo might not be easily fetchable via webfetch. Let me try.\n\nLet me also search for the gismo config. Let me use grep on the saved tool output? No, that's the ar5iv paper. I need to fetch the gismo repo's conf files and the gismo README.\n\nLet me fetch:\n1. https://github.com/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/conf (or raw files)\n2. https://github.com/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/gismo\n3. https://bitbucket.org/iAnalytica/ingredient-substitution\n4. Search for Hyperfoods ERC project.\n\nLet me do these in parallel."
